 of college and career readiness, such as graduation rates, college entrance exams, and advanced courses.\\n\\nEven at schools with strong college and career readiness, there may be students who are not getting the opportunities they need to succeed.\\n\",\"schoolGranularRatingsDescription\":\"The College Readiness Rating uses this high school\\u0027s graduation rates, college entrance exam participation and performance, or AP, IB, or Dual Enrollment participation to determine how well schools are preparing students for success in college and beyond. The College Readiness Rating was created using the following data from the 2021 Civil Rights Data Collection: percentage of students enrolled in IB, AP or Dual Enrollment classes in grades 9-12, using 2023 4-year high school graduation rate data from Arizona Department of Education, using 2024 ACT percent college ready data from Arizona Department of Education, and using 2023 demographic data from the National Center for Education Statistics.\"},{\"schoolId\":391173,\"dataSourceId\":633,\"schoolGranularRatingType\":\"Student Growth\",\"schoolGranularRatingValue\":\"5\",\"schoolGranularRatingCopyText\":\"Students at this school are making average academic progress from one grade to the next compared to similar students in the state.\",\"schoolGranularRatingsDescription\":\"The Student Progress Rating measures whether students at this school are making academic progress over time based on student growth data provided by the Department of Education. Specifically, this rating looks at how much progress individual students have made on state assessments during the past year or more, how this performance aligns with expected progress based on a student growth model established by the state Department of Education, and how this school\\u0027s growth data compares to other schools in the state. The Growth Rating was created using 2024 Student growth data from Arizona Department of Education.\"},{\"schoolId\":391172,\"dataSourceId\":633,\"schoolGranularRatingType\":\"Test Scores\",\"schoolGranularRatingValue\":\"4\",\"schoolGranularRatingCopyText\":\"State test results at this school are below the state average, so students are likely performing below grade level.\",\"schoolGranularRatingsDescription\":\"The Test Score Rating examines how students at this school performed on standardized tests compared with other schools in the state. The Test Rating was created using 2024 Arizona Academic Standards Assessment data from Arizona Department of Education, and using 2024 Arizona Science Field Test data from Arizona Department of Education.\"},{\"schoolId\":241202,\"dataSourceId\":633,\"schoolGranularRatingType\":\"Equity\",\"schoolGranularRatingValue\":\"5\",\"schoolGranularRatingCopyText\":\"Underserved students at this school are performing about as well as other students in the state, but this school may still have achievement gaps between different student groups.\",\"schoolGranularRatingsDescription\":\"Using the state’s Department of Education data, the Equity Overview Rating compares this school to other schools in the state by looking at how well this school serves the needs of disadvantaged students relative to all students using state proficiency tests, student growth or academic progress data, and college readiness data. The Equity Rating was created using 2023 4-year high school graduation rate data from Arizona Department of Education, using 2024 Student growth data from Arizona Department of Education, using 2024 Arizona Academic Standards Assessment data from Arizona Department of Education, using 2024 Arizona Science Field Test data from Arizona Department of Education, and using 2023 demographic data from the National Center for Education Statistics.\"}],\"schoolDistrict\":{\"id\":6173,\"districtName\":\"Gilbert Unified District\",\"address\":\"1016 North Burk Street\",\"city\":\"Gilbert\",\"stateCode\":\"AZ\",\"zip\":\"85234\",\"latitude\":33.368919,\"longitude\":-111.7826,\"websiteUrl\":\"http:\u002F\u002Fwww.gilbertschools.net\",\"greatschoolDistrictOverviewUrl\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fgilbert\u002Fgilbert-unified-district\u002F\"},\"greatschoolParentReviewsUrl\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fgilbert\u002F727-Gilbert-High-School\u002F#Reviews\",\"elementary\":false,\"middle\":true,\"high\":true,\"lastUpdatedDate\":\"April 2025\",\"hasMultipleCatchmentAreas\":false},{\"servesHome\":false,\"greatSchoolsRating\":8,\"parentRating\":3,\"distanceInMiles\":\"2.3\",\"gradeRanges\":\"7-12\",\"institutionType\":\"Public\",\"name\":\"Gilbert Classical Academy High School\",\"schoolUrl\":\"\u002Fschool\u002F185164\u002FAZ\u002FGilbert\u002FGilbert-Classical-Academy-High-School\",\"searchUrl\":\"\u002Fschool\u002F185164\u002FAZ\u002FGilbert\u002FGilbert-Classical-Academy-High-School\",\"greatSchoolOverviewUrl\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fgilbert\u002F3622-Gilbert-Classical-Academy-High-School\u002F\",\"id\":185164,\"numberOfStudents\":596,\"fullAddress\":\"1016 N Burk St, Gilbert, AZ 85234\",\"isNearby\":true,\"numReviews\":41,\"studentToTeacherRatio\":13,\"websiteUrl\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fgilbertclassicalacademy.gilbertschools.net\u002F\",\"schoolReviews\":[{\"schoolId\":43355561,\"reviewedBy\":\"Parent\",\"datePosted\":\"May 2025\",\"review\":\"Yes, students must be high academic achievers to succeed. No problem there. However, the teachers should still TEACH. My child has attended GCA for 2 years now, and each year, about 1\u002F3 of the teachers are atrocious. They hand students a packet and tell them to do it without showing them how to do so. One Algebra teacher actually makes fun of students when they don\\u0027t understand something. THIS IS NOT TEACHING. The other 2\u002F3 of the teachers are amazing. My child has truly learned things in those classes, and talks about them at home. The other issue is lack of athletics. They do well in certain sports, but if football or basketball are your thing, look elsewhere. I also think it\\u0027s ridiculous that a supposed college prep school does not offer dual enrollment courses. Finally, seniors do not get the common half days you hear about so often because GCA requires more credits for graduation. This school has so much potential. It\\u0027s sad to see low enrollment and students leaving. If they want to increase enrollment, they should try listening to the parents and students. I do love the community, the camaraderie, and small size of the school. I\\u0027ve never heard about any bullying.\",\"reviewerRating\":3,\"lastUpdatedDate\":\"June 2025\",\"institutionGreatschoolId\":403622,\"maponicsId\":6968642,\"url\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fgilbert\u002F3622-Gilbert-Classical-Academy-High-School\u002F\"},{\"schoolId\":43355560,\"reviewedBy\":\"Parent\",\"datePosted\":\"April 2025\",\"review\":\"Both of my children have thrived academically, socially, and athletically. We have been so grateful for the opportunity for them to attend Gilbert Classical Academy!\",\"reviewerRating\":5,\"lastUpdatedDate\":\"June 2025\",\"institutionGreatschoolId\":403622,\"maponicsId\":6883495,\"url\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fgilbert\u002F3622-Gilbert-Classical-Academy-High-School\u002F\"},{\"schoolId\":43355559,\"reviewedBy\":\"Parent\",\"datePosted\":\"March 2025\",\"review\":\"The school focuses on college preparedness and not a sense of community or self expression. If you have a child that requires social interaction and freedom of self expression to flourish, this is not the school for you. The uniform policy is stringent and the staff does not enforce the dress code uniformly. One teacher may let a dress code infraction slide and another may remove the child from class for not adhering to the policy. This is explained several times during new student orientation and emails from staff through the year. Given this is a public school, you would believe their expectations would be more laxed, yet that is not the case. The focus is making certain all students fall in line and not celebrating and growing your teens character and self confidence in, what one may call, their most formidable years. I\\u0027ve had more than one child enrolled in this school and have seen the bias first hand when you have a child that is more colorful, creative, and self expressive than that of children that accomodate and adapt. I don\\u0027t believe that a child\\u0027s personality should be dampened to maintain an above average school rating with conventionalist pupils. While this is a college preparatory school, counselors lack in guidance and support for students and parents who are new to the college application process. One of my students found it difficult when working with counselors to create an academic plan post graduation even though they had the grit and grades to succeed at a university. My child felt that the guidance counselors focused their attention on the students and parents that were prepared with an academic or career path and not to those who required additional planning or support.In my experience, this is a school for students who are ready for college and not for students that excel in studies but haven\\u0027t figured out their career path. It is emphasized early on in registration and orientations that this is a challenging school with a rigorous curriculum, and that is fact. If you have a student that conforms and keeps their nose to the grindstone, they will thrive at this school. If your child is not 100% decided on a college, the lack of support and compassion is obvious and unfortunate. As a parent, I would question the rate at which students drop out or switch schools before registering your student here. While having a highly rated high school looks great for college admissions, it does not come without high expectations or added stress.\",\"reviewerRating\":3,\"lastUpdatedDate\":\"June 2025\",\"institutionGreatschoolId\":403622,\"maponicsId\":6863309,\"url\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fgilbert\u002F3622-Gilbert-Classical-Academy-High-School\u002F\"},{\"schoolId\":43355558,\"reviewedBy\":\"Student\",\"datePosted\":\"March 2025\",\"review\":\"I really appreciate this school for its challenging approach. Despite the occasional tough moments, they help us become better thinkers and leaders. There\\u0027s a common misconception that the skills we develop here aren\\u0027t useful in the real world, but GCA is designed for college-prep. So, if you don\\u0027t plan to go to college, GCA just might not be the right fit for you.Unlike other schools, GCA demands hard work to succeed. The results speak for themselves: a remarkable 100% graduation rate to prestigious colleges like Harvard and Yale.It\\u0027s reassuring to know that GCA fosters an atmosphere of respect and collaboration. A huge benefit of attending GCA is the small campus size, which allows us to get to know our classmates and peers on a personal level. This creates a tight-knit community where teachers and students are able to form meaningful relationships. In contrast, larger schools often struggle to establish such connections among their students. We are lucky to have such a peaceful and tight-knit place to grow and learn where any sort of conflict is extremely rare and if any sort arises it is typically very small.\",\"reviewerRating\":5,\"lastUpdatedDate\":\"June 2025\",\"institutionGreatschoolId\":403622,\"maponicsId\":6852047,\"url\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fgilbert\u002F3622-Gilbert-Classical-Academy-High-School\u002F\"},{\"schoolId\":43355557,\"reviewedBy\":\"Parent\",\"datePosted\":\"March 2025\",\"review\":\"GCA is challenging, and it does require hard work, but the students and staff have fun, bond, and the students are extremely successful in the next phase of life.\",\"reviewerRating\":5,\"las